# interplay_memlive_alias_page_table: Task 2 maps task 1's page table as data: its VA page 10 is task 1's (only) table page. Task 2 copies the table out (it equals the guest's table), then writes leaves into it with the GPU: a blit copy of a u32 from its own buffer to entry 12 points task 1's VA page 12 (buffer B, never made) at another page, and one to entry 5 points task 1's command-buffer page 5 at a page holding another segment. Task 1's next execs walk the tables the GPU wrote: B is made over the new page and the other segment runs, in every setup (the blocks setup's walks read guest RAM through read_memory, which the GPU's write reached). Last, task 1's read of buffer C (VA 13, never made) waits on the gate while task 2, on the worker FIFO, rewrites entry 13: released, C is made over the page task 2 wrote.
